  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Leidos is a federal contractor with $2B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Leidos received 2,734 awards so far in the fiscal year, and the average award size is $730K. Leidos obligations are down 34.3% year over year. Leidos obligations by fiscal year show a peak at $3B in FY24 and $3B in FY25 before falling to $2B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.5B in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services and Computer Facilities Management Services are the top NAICS markets for Leidos, with $635M and $538M respectively. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance follow with $299M and $227M. Leidos also shows activity in Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $131M and in Other Individual and Family Services at $79.5M. Smaller-dollar markets include Research and Development categories and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $5K. The dataset notes that award-value figures in some tables are total contract values and that current-year totals are partial fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Leidos' federal obligation trend changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Leidos obligations were $1.9B in FY21, rose to $2.7B in FY22, and totaled $2.6B in FY23. Leidos obligations peaked at $3B in FY24 and remained $3B in FY25 before falling to $2B in FY26. Leidos year-over-year change for FY2026 to date is down 34.3%."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies account for the largest share of Leidos' FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B to Leidos in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Transportation follow with $233M and $131M respectively. The General Services Administration obligated $79.5M, and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $50.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
