    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Leidos?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys the most from Leidos, with $1.5B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other buying agencies include the Department of Homeland Security at $233M, the Department of Transportation at $131M, the General Services Administration at $79.5M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $50.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Leidos sell to the government?",
      "a": "Leidos sells services in several NAICS markets, led by Computer Systems Design Services at $635M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $538M. Leidos also sells Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $299M, Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $227M, and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $131M, among other categories."
